{% comment %}
  One selectable row in the Concern Select step's list. This step is a
  replacement for a free-text "what are you coming in for" field, not a
  doctor filter/search — so a row is just an icon, the concern name, and a
  checkbox. No doctor count.

  Multi-select (checkbox), not single-select — updated to match the
  revised Figma spec, which shows a checkbox per row and no
  default-selected concern. Was previously a radio-style single select
  with "General Medicine" pre-selected; see kal-booking-flow.js's
  concernSelect state (now a Set, toggled per row) for the corresponding
  JS change.

  Accepts:
  - icon_name: {String} passed to kal-booking-icons (one of the 'concern-*' icons)
  - name: {String} e.g. "General Wellness"
  - concern_key: {String} value for data-kal-concern, e.g. "general-wellness" —
    matched against the concernSelect JS state to drive the checkbox state
  - selected: {Boolean} true if this concern should start checked (none do,
    per the current spec — kept as a param in case that changes later)

  Usage:
  {% render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-general-medicine', name: 'General Wellness', concern_key: 'general-wellness', selected: false %}
{% endcomment %}

<button
  type="button"
  class="kal-concern-row {% if selected %}kal-concern-row--selected{% endif %}"
  data-kal-concern="{{ concern_key }}"
  aria-pressed="{{ selected }}"
>
  <span class="kal-concern-row__left">
    <span class="kal-concern-row__icon">
      {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: icon_name -%}
    </span>
    <span class="kal-concern-row__name">{{ name }}</span>
  </span>
  <span class="kal-concern-row__checkbox" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
  </span>
</button>
